    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the read-time `riskFlag` field on the owner response so it's `true` when **any** of the three conditions hold, else `false`.\n\n**What the three conditions map to:**\n\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 `owner.getPossibleDuplicate() == true` (already assigned at creation by `AssignPossibleDuplicate`).\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2014 the email's second-level label (`mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`) matches a known disposable provider, regardless of TLD or subdomain. Since exactly-disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, etc.) are already rejected with 400 at create time by `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, this catches the neighbours it lets through (e.g. `mailinator.org`, `inbox.mailinator.com`).\n3. **City over its soft capacity** \u2014 the city already holds at least 40 owners (the existing per-city warning threshold, now named `CITY_SOFT_CAPACITY`). Unlike the existing `capacityWarning`, this stays true at/above the hard limit of 50.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema (generates `getRiskFlag`/`setRiskFlag` on `OwnerDto`), with a description documenting all three conditions.\n- `OwnerCityCapacity.java` \u2014 added `CITY_SOFT_CAPACITY` and `isOverSoftCapacity(...)`, reusing the existing city-count logic.\n- `OwnerRiskFlag.java` (new) \u2014 the derivation helper, centralizing the three-way OR and the disposable-adjacent domain check.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 `@Mapping(target = \"riskFlag\", ignore = true)` (set explicitly by the responders, like the other derived warnings).\n- `RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`, `RespondWithExistingOwner` \u2014 set `riskFlag` alongside the existing `capacityWarning`/`bulkSignupWarning`, so it appears on the GET, create, update, and idempotent-replay responses consistently.\n\nThe new `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` acceptance test (unique city, no email, no duplicate \u2192 `false`) passes, and the full suite stays green.",
